flowchart LR
  accTitle: Public, owner, and producer authority lanes
  accDescr: Canonical projections can serve all three audience lanes. Transcript reads are filtered for each audience. Selected thinking and strategy can enter a viewer-safe public projection, while underlying cognitive artifacts require subject, participant, or producer policy. Private traces reach producer diagnostics only.

  Canonical["Canonical projections"] --> Public["Public and viewer lane"]
  Canonical --> Owner["Subject owner and participant lane"]
  Canonical --> Producer["Producer and admin lane"]

  Transcript["Authorized transcript"] --> Public
  Transcript --> Owner
  Transcript --> Producer

  Cognition["Cognitive artifacts"] -->|viewer-safe projection| Public
  Cognition -->|artifact and subject policy| Owner
  Cognition -->|producer policy| Producer

  Trace["Private trace evidence"] -->|producer scope plus current role| Producer

  Public --> PublicUse["Watch state, dialogue, selected cognition, profiles, results"]
  Owner --> OwnerUse["Owned cognition and participant-authorized context"]
  Producer --> ProducerUse["Diagnostics, wider analysis, bounded raw evidence"]

  class Canonical truthNode
  class Transcript viewNode
  class Cognition cognitionNode
  class Trace evidenceNode
  class Public,Owner,Producer laneNode
  class PublicUse,OwnerUse,ProducerUse outputNode

  classDef truthNode fill:#052e16,stroke:#4ade80,color:#f0fdf4,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef viewNode fill:#083344,stroke:#22d3ee,color:#ecfeff,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef cognitionNode fill:#3f2b08,stroke:#facc15,color:#fefce8,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef evidenceNode fill:#431407,stroke:#fb923c,color:#fff7ed,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef laneNode fill:#3b0764,stroke:#c084fc,color:#faf5ff,stroke-width:1.5px
